# {{ appKey }} App

## Start with this App

- Read `nexia.json`, `README.md`, `docs/README.md`, and relevant App-owned docs
  for identity, commands, and domain rules. Inspect the affected source and
  callers before editing; preserve existing work, migrations, and data.
- Work only in this App using installed public SDK contracts. Do not import,
  copy, or patch Core, another App, or installed dependencies. Report a missing
  public capability through developer support without exposing credentials or data.
- Check the installed SDK versions and target host compatibility before using a
  contract. Read only the relevant guides below; use `nexia docs search "topic"`
  and `nexia docs read <document-id>` or the linked website when needed.

## Choose guidance for the task

| Task | Read before implementation |
| --- | --- |
| Frontend screens and CSS | https://developers.nexia.to/docs/building-apps-build-a-frontend-surface and https://developers.nexia.to/docs/app-sdk-frontend-host-contracts and see https://developers.nexia.to/examples |
| Resource, data model and migration | https://developers.nexia.to/docs/building-apps-create-a-resource and https://developers.nexia.to/docs/building-apps-data-model-and-migrations |
| API, actor and authorization | https://developers.nexia.to/docs/building-apps-add-api-and-authorization |
| Cross-App data and batching | https://developers.nexia.to/docs/platform-extensions-resource-references |
| Events and background work | https://developers.nexia.to/docs/building-apps-handle-events-and-async-work |
| Translation catalogs | https://developers.nexia.to/docs/building-apps-localize-an-app |
| Testing and release | https://developers.nexia.to/docs/building-apps-test-an-app and https://developers.nexia.to/docs/building-apps-release-an-app |

For frontend work, prefer existing public `@nexia/sdk/host` components and
patterns whenever they meet the need. Use their supported props and slots;
scope custom styles to App-owned markup instead of overriding host internals.
For cross-App list references, batch unique IDs for the authorized page and
preserve actor, organization, date, and purpose boundaries. Follow the guide's
compatibility and fallback rules; do not retry omitted IDs as an access bypass.
For translations, reuse supported host `common.*` keys for shared UI and keep
App-owned domain wording in flat App catalogs. Fix validation errors before
retrying; never delete `.nexia` or reset data to bypass recovery status.

## App-owned guidance and delivery

Maintain this file with the App's domain constraints, conventions, and focused
checks. Keep shared platform details in the linked guides. Existing App files
and instructions belong to their developer and are not replaced by tool updates.

Use the checks in README.md. At validation, start with relevant `nexia check`,
`nexia test`, or `nexia test --frontend`, then verify changed behavior and
permissions in the sandbox. Report source checks and observed runtime behavior
separately. Draft changes defer automated checks until testing, verification,
finalization, commit, push, or PR is requested. Never commit, push, submit,
merge, publish, reset data, or send messages without authorization.
